From fe40ba400638e2e334d2317504c0007b598ada38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ws07 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:16:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Web client: the turn's length and the season's deadlines
 from the season, not from the words
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Connection patch of workstream 07 (player experience), brief item 4 and
claim 5.

The glossary, the first card and the title wrote 「10分ごと」 into their
sentences: on a local world whose clock runs 10× or 40× faster a turn lasts
a minute or fifteen seconds, and the words said otherwise. No screen named
the season's join deadline (Season.joinCloseBell), and a join after it was
refused with the generic WrongStatus. frontier/seasonterms.mjs words a
turn from BELL_SECS and the chain's pace (on a faster clock, the real time
too) and reads the deadlines from the season; the join screen says them and,
once joining closed, turns its button off with the cause. Three tests that
pinned the old sentences now pin the new ones.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C5Nj2bNLFpFghsNM9fsQG5
